  {
    "sha": "95005b14544e3f03f73eb465054d9cbb1f7de0b6",
    "node_id": "C_kwDOVoU8JdoAKDk1MDA1YjE0NTQ0ZTNmMDNmNzNlYjQ2NTA1NGQ5Y2JiMWY3ZGUwYjY",
    "commit": {
      "author": {
        "name": "Mike Kinney",
        "email": "mike.kinney@gmail.com",
        "date": "2026-11-12T22:55:46Z"
      },
      "committer": {
        "name": "Mike Kinney",
        "email": "mike.kinney@gmail.com",
        "date": "2026-11-12T22:55:46Z"
      },
      "message": "fix(ui): console std handles after attach; error box with no console\n\nReview of PR #1287: after a successful AttachConsole, point each NULL or\ninvalid stdout/stderr handle at CONOUT$ (valid ones - redirects, pipes -\nare left alone), so std::io::stderr (tracing) reaches the terminal. With no\nconsole attached, show a MessageBoxW when run returns non-zero and from a\npanic hook chained after the previous one (one box per process). All new\ncode is cfg(windows) in crates/ui/src/win_console.rs, via extern \"system\"\ndeclarations (no new dependency). Log file with no console: #1323.\n\nRefs #1278\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>",
